            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hablasteis. Now the other two families, and then the hard stems."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: -isteis, for everything else",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "comer, comisteis.",
                "vivir, vivisteis."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One ending for both, exactly as everywhere else in the preterite. The -er and -ir families stopped being two families the first time you met this tense."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: and the strong stems take it too",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The stems that gave you trouble — tuv-, hic-, estuv-, dij- — take the same -isteis, with no surprises left in them:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tuvisteis, hicisteis, estuvisteis, dijisteis."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And ser/ir, which share one past: fuisteis."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That was the last hole. The preterite is finished — every family, every person, regular and strong alike, with nothing outstanding."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It has taken a long stretch of this book to build, and it is the largest single structure in it. The review that named this debt out loud can now be read without a caveat."
            }
          ]
        },
